# hand.ges — a hand on the roll's notes: press, drag, release, as a chart.
#
# The fourth chart `chart.ges` runs and the second gesture, built
# 2026-09-08 (`card:gui-is-difficult.md` §"Landed — 2026-09-08": the
# note hand, reading A — *the hit-test's answer rides on the event*).
# Where `gesture.ges` is a hand on one thing, this is a hand on a roll:
# a press decides three things by looking — a note under it, a note's
# end, or empty roll — and the chart cannot look, so **the host looks
# and the touch carries what it found** (`Hit`).  The chart then holds
# the one thing it is for: what the press became, and what a later
# touch or the release means because of it.
#
# **A press on the roll is two touches.**  The window walks the pad's
# two halves in order — the rail writes a tick, then the pitch half
# writes a key — so the chart has a state between them, `Railed`, and
# the pitch's touch is the one that carries the hit.  A pitch touch
# with no rail before it is ignored: the rail speaks first.
#
# The host holds the geometry and the group: a tick arrives as the
# roll's own tick and is snapped to the grid where it is used; whether
# `Carry` means one note or the selected group is the host's, because
# the group is the model's and not the hand's.

# ── What the pitch half found ────────────────────────────────────────────

#: Under the press: a note, its end, or nothing — the host's hit test,
#: on the event.
Hit := OnNote Int | OnEnd Int | OnRoll

# ── The states ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#: Nothing held; the rail has spoken a tick and the pitch half is next;
#: a note held where it was taken (note, tick, key); the note carried
#: from there to here (note, tick0, key0, tick, key); a note's end held
#: at a tick; the end carried (note, tick0, tick); empty roll pressed
#: at a corner; the band swept to the other corner.
Hand := Free
      | Railed Int
      | Held Int Int Int
      | Carried Int Int Int Int Int
      | Ending Int Int
      | Ended Int Int Int
      | Sweeping Int Int
      | Swept Int Int Int Int

# ── The touches and the acts ─────────────────────────────────────────────

#: The rail's touch at a tick; the pitch half's touch at a key, with
#: what was under it; the grab let go; the gesture abandoned.
Touch := Rail Int | Pitch Int Hit | Lift | Abort

#: What the host does.  `Grab` on taking a note — select it, say its
#: line; `Shift` while carried — preview both axes; `Click` when let go
#: where it was taken — reveal; `Carry` when let go after moving — the
#: commit, `transpose`, `move` or `carry` by the host's reading of the
#: group; `GrabEnd`, `Grow`, `Resize` the same three for a note's end;
#: `Sweep` and `Select` the band's preview and commit; `Clear` on
#: pressing empty roll at a corner — nothing is selected any more, and
#: the hand is told what a sweep does; `Drop` — put the picture back.
Act := Grab Int Int Int
     | Shift Int Int Int Int Int
     | Click Int
     | Carry Int Int Int Int Int
     | GrabEnd Int Int
     | Grow Int Int Int
     | Resize Int Int Int
     | Sweep Int Int Int Int
     | Select Int Int Int Int
     | Clear Int Int
     | Drop

# ── The chart ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

hand : Chart Hand Touch Act
hand = Chart Free handStep handEnter

#: Thirty-two arrows, all written.  The rail's touch while free is the
#: first half of a press; the pitch's touch after it decides which of
#: three hands this is; every touch after that carries the latest
#: place on its own axis; a release is a click from a held state and a
#: commit from a carried one; an abort lands free from anywhere.
handStep : Hand -> Touch -> Step Hand Act
handStep Free (Rail t) = Go (Railed t) []
handStep Free (Pitch k h) = Stay
handStep Free Lift = Stay
handStep Free Abort = Stay
handStep (Railed t) (Rail u) = Go (Railed u) []
handStep (Railed t) (Pitch k (OnNote n)) = Go (Held n t k) []
handStep (Railed t) (Pitch k (OnEnd n)) = Go (Ending n t) []
handStep (Railed t) (Pitch k OnRoll) = Go (Sweeping t k) []
handStep (Railed t) Lift = Go Free []
handStep (Railed t) Abort = Go Free []
handStep (Held n t k) (Rail u) = Go (Carried n t k u k) [Shift n t k u k]
handStep (Held n t k) (Pitch q h) = Go (Carried n t k t q) [Shift n t k t q]
handStep (Held n t k) Lift = Go Free [Click n]
handStep (Held n t k) Abort = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Carried n t k u q) (Rail v) = Go (Carried n t k v q) [Shift n t k v q]
handStep (Carried n t k u q) (Pitch r h) = Go (Carried n t k u r) [Shift n t k u r]
handStep (Carried n t k u q) Lift = Go Free [Carry n t k u q]
handStep (Carried n t k u q) Abort = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Ending n t) (Rail u) = Go (Ended n t u) [Grow n t u]
handStep (Ending n t) (Pitch q h) = Stay
handStep (Ending n t) Lift = Go Free [Click n]
handStep (Ending n t) Abort = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Ended n t u) (Rail v) = Go (Ended n t v) [Grow n t v]
handStep (Ended n t u) (Pitch q h) = Stay
handStep (Ended n t u) Lift = Go Free [Resize n t u]
handStep (Ended n t u) Abort = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Sweeping t k) (Rail u) = Go (Swept t k u k) [Sweep t k u k]
handStep (Sweeping t k) (Pitch q h) = Go (Swept t k t q) [Sweep t k t q]
handStep (Sweeping t k) Lift = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Sweeping t k) Abort = Go Free [Drop]
handStep (Swept t k u q) (Rail v) = Go (Swept t k v q) [Sweep t k v q]
handStep (Swept t k u q) (Pitch r h) = Go (Swept t k u r) [Sweep t k u r]
handStep (Swept t k u q) Lift = Go Free [Select t k u q]
handStep (Swept t k u q) Abort = Go Free [Drop]

#: Taking hold is an entry action, so it happens once, on the arrow in.
handEnter : Hand -> List Act
handEnter (Held n t k) = [Grab n t k]
handEnter (Ending n t) = [GrabEnd n t]
handEnter (Sweeping t k) = [Clear t k]
handEnter h = []
